
  Hacking Kubernetes — study lab VM

  One machine, every capability: Docker, k3s (NetworkPolicy enforced),
  gVisor sandbox runtime, Falco sensor. Labs are deployed into it one at
  a time from the host.

  hk-lab list            every lab and whether it is deployed here
  hk-lab check           re-check the VM's capabilities
  hk-lab status <lab>    what a lab has created so far
  hk-lab reset <lab>     clear what a lab created, restore its files

  lab 4                  jump to Lab 4's working directory
  k, new_lab             the Lab 0 helpers, already defined

  Working copies   ~/labs/labNN/          (edit freely)
  Pristine kits    /opt/hk-labs/labNN/    (reset source)

  From the host:
    hk deploy lab04      add a lab to this VM
    hk remove lab04      take it out again

